# Single read-only index submodule.
#
# 2026-08-18: every cloud-* repo embeds ONLY `cloud` — the fleet index,
# formerly cloud-master. https:// rather than git@ makes it read-only in
# practice: the index is consumed here, never pushed from here.
#
# No recursion: `cloud` declares no submodules of its own — it indexes the
# fleet with committed RELATIVE symlinks, which dangle harmlessly inside a
# submodule checkout. `cloud` is public, so init needs no credentials.
#
# The ship engine reconciles declaratively against this file: declared-but-
# unregistered gets `git submodule add`, registered-but-undeclared gets
# `git rm --cached`. Deleting this section removes the submodule.

[submodule "I_cloud"]
	path = I_cloud
	url = git@github.com:diegonmarcos/cloud.git
	shallow = true
	ignore = all

# 2026-09-06: a_solutions is NOT a submodule and must not be re-added as one.
#
# It was split out to diegonmarcos/cloud-u-containers on 2026-08-27 and then
# immediately mounted back here as a submodule, which kept every path
# resolving but left the tree inside cloud-infra in every way that mattered:
# a container change still had to land here as a gitlink bump, so this repo
# still gated, versioned and triggered on it. It is now a plain sibling
# repository, checked out by CI at the path `a_solutions` with
# actions/checkout (see 1_cicd/src/cicd/*.yml) and cloned standalone into
# ~/git/cloud-u-containers for local work. The ~400 in-repo references still
# resolve because the checkout PATH is unchanged — only the ownership moved.
#
# Consequences, so nobody "fixes" this by re-adding the section:
#   • No `paths: a_solutions` filter can ever fire again — no file and no
#     gitlink for it exists here. Container pushes arrive as a
#     `repository_dispatch` of type `containers-push` sent by
#     cloud-u-containers/.github/workflows/dispatch-cloud-infra.yml.
#   • Per-service change detection diffs client_payload.{before,after}
#     INSIDE the a_solutions checkout, not a gitlink in this repo.
#   • a_solutions/ is gitignored here so the untracked checkout cannot be
#     swept into a commit by a bulk `git add`.
